# **1. Gear Analysis:**\n\n* Calculate the gear ratio ($i$).\n\n\n* Calculate the output speed ($\\text{RPM}_{\\text{out}}$) of Gear B.\n\n\n* Calculate the output torque ($T_{\\text{out}}$) available at the output shaft in $\\text{N}\\cdot\\text{m}$.\n\n\n\n#### **2. Shaft Analysis:**\n\n* If the output shaft transmits this output torque ($T_{\\text{out}}$) and is subjected to an equivalent bending moment of $M = 250\\text{ N}\\cdot\\text{m}$, calculate the minimum required shaft diameter ($d$) using the von Mises shear stress criterion.\n\n\n\n#### **3. Material Specification:**\n\n* The shaft is made of steel with an allowable shear stress ($\\tau_{\\text{allow}}$) of **$50\\text{ MPa}$**.'}], 'model': 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 'n': 1, 'reasoning_effort': None, 'reasoning_format': None, 'service_tier': 'on_demand', 'stop': None, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.7, 'tools': [{'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_force', 'description': "Calculate force using Newton's second law.\n\nFormula:\n    F = m * a\n\nArgs:\n    mass: Mass in kilograms (kg).\n    acceleration: Acceleration in meters per second squared (m/s²).\n\nReturns:\n    Force in Newtons (N).", 'parameters': {'properties': {'mass': {'type': 'number'}, 'acceleration': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['mass', 'acceleration'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_mass', 'description': 'Calculate mass from force and acceleration.\n\nFormula:\n    m = F / a\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    acceleration: Acceleration in meters per second squared (m/s²).\n\nReturns:\n    Mass in kilograms (kg).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'acceleration': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'acceleration'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_acceleration', 'description': 'Calculate acceleration from force and mass.\n\nFormula:\n    a = F / m\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    mass: Mass in kilograms (kg).\n\nReturns:\n    Acceleration in meters per second squared (m/s²).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'mass': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'mass'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_torque', 'description': 'Calculate torque.\n\nFormula:\n    τ = r * F * sin(θ)\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    lever_arm: Distance from pivot in meters (m).\n    angle: Angle between force and lever arm in degrees.\n\nReturns:\n    Torque in Newton-meters (N·m).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'lever_arm': {'type': 'number'}, 'angle': {'default': 90.0, 'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'lever_arm'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_work', 'description': 'Calculate mechanical work.\n\nFormula:\n    W = F * d * cos(θ)\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    displacement: Displacement in meters (m).\n    angle: Angle between force and displacement in degrees.\n\nReturns:\n    Work in Joules (J).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'displacement': {'type': 'number'}, 'angle': {'default': 0.0, 'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'displacement'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_energy', 'description': 'Calculate kinetic energy.\n\nFormula:\n    KE = 1/2 * m * v²\n\nArgs:\n    mass: Mass in kilograms (kg).\n    velocity: Velocity in meters per second (m/s).\n\nReturns:\n    Kinetic energy in Joules (J).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'mass': {'type': 'number'}, 'velocity': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['mass', 'velocity'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_power', 'description': 'Calculate mechanical power.\n\nFormula:\n    P = W / t\n\nArgs:\n    work: Work in Joules (J).\n    time: Time in seconds (s).\n\nReturns:\n    Power in Watts (W).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'work': {'type': 'number'}, 'time': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['work', 'time'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_stress', 'description': 'Calculate normal stress.\n\nFormula:\n    σ = F / A\n\nArgs:\n    force: Force in Newtons (N).\n    area: Cross-sectional area in square meters (m²).\n\nReturns:\n    Stress in Pascals (Pa).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'force': {'type': 'number'}, 'area': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['force', 'area'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'calculate_strain', 'description': 'Calculate normal strain.\n\nFormula:\n    ε = ΔL / L₀\n\nArgs:\n    change_in_length: Change in length in meters (m).\n    original_length: Original length in meters (m).\n\nReturns:\n    Strain (dimensionless).', 'parameters': {'properties': {'change_in_length': {'type': 'number'}, 'original_length': {'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['change_in_length', 'original_length'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'shaft_design', 'description': 'Design and analyze a solid circular shaft under torque and bending loads.\n\nSupported operations:\n\n1. shaft_diameter\n   Calculate required shaft diameter considering combined bending\n   and torsional loading.\n\n   Bending stress:\n       sigma = 32*M / (pi*d^3)\n\n   Torsional shear stress:\n       tau = 16*T / (pi*d^3)\n\n   Von Mises equivalent stress:\n       sigma_vm = sqrt(sigma^2 + 3*tau^2)\n\n   Required diameter:\n       d = [\n           (16 / (pi * allowable_stress))\n           * sqrt(4*M^2 + 3*T^2)\n       ]^(1/3)\n\n   Requires:\n       torque\n       bending_moment\n       allowable_stress\n\n2. torsional_stress\n   Calculate torsional shear stress in a solid circular shaft.\n\n       tau = 16*T / (pi*d^3)\n\n   Requires:\n       torque\n       diameter\n\n3. shear_stress\n   Calculate combined transverse and torsional shear stress.\n\n   Torsional shear:\n       tau_t = 16*T / (pi*d^3)\n\n   Average transverse shear:\n       tau_v = F / A\n\n   Conservative combined shear:\n       tau_total = tau_t + tau_v\n\n   Requires:\n       torque\n       diameter\n       transverse_force\n       area\n\n4. factor_of_safety\n   Calculate factor of safety using Von Mises stress.\n\n       sigma_b = 32*M / (pi*d^3)\n\n       tau_t = 16*T / (pi*d^3)\n\n       sigma_vm = sqrt(sigma_b^2 + 3*tau_t^2)\n\n       FoS = yield_strength / sigma_vm\n\n   Requires:\n       torque\n       bending_moment\n       diameter\n       yield_strength\n\nImportant:\n    All quantities must use a consistent unit system.\n\n    Example:\n        torque     -> N*m\n        bending    -> N*m\n        diameter   -> m\n        stress     -> Pa\n        yield      -> Pa\n\n    This implementation assumes a solid circular shaft.', 'parameters': {'properties': {'operation': {'enum': ['shaft_diameter', 'torsional_stress', 'shear_stress', 'factor_of_safety'], 'type': 'string'}, 'torque': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'bending_moment': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'diameter': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'allowable_stress': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'yield_strength': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'transverse_force': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'area': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}}, 'required': ['operation'], 'type': 'object'}}}, {'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'gear_design', 'description': 'Calculate gear ratio, output speed, output torque, or mechanical power.\n\nGear ratio:\n    GR = N_output / N_input\n\nFor an ideal gear pair:\n\n    n_output = n_input / GR\n\n    T_output = T_input * GR\n\nWith efficiency:\n\n    T_output = T_input * GR * efficiency\n\nMechanical power:\n\n    P = T * omega\n\nwhere:\n\n    omega = 2*pi*n / 60\n\nTherefore:\n\n    P = T * 2*pi*n / 60\n\nInputs:\n    input_speed:\n        Input shaft speed in RPM.\n\n    output_speed_value:\n        Output shaft speed in RPM.\n        Used when calculating gear ratio.\n\n    input_torque:\n        Input torque in N*m.\n\n    output_torque_value:\n        Output torque in N*m.\n        Used when calculating gear ratio from torque.\n\n    input_teeth:\n        Number of teeth on the driving/input gear.\n\n    output_teeth:\n        Number of teeth on the driven/output gear.\n\n    efficiency:\n        Gear transmission efficiency from 0 to 1.\n        Example:\n            0.95 = 95% efficiency.\n\nNotes:\n    - All speeds are RPM.\n    - Torque is N*m.\n    - Power is returned in Watts.\n    - For gear_ratio, teeth are preferred because they directly\n      determine the ratio.\n    - This tool assumes two externally meshing gears.', 'parameters': {'properties': {'operation': {'enum': ['gear_ratio', 'output_speed', 'output_torque', 'power'], 'type': 'string'}, 'input_speed': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'output_speed_value': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'input_torque': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'output_torque_value': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'number'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'input_teeth': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'integer'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'output_teeth': {'anyOf': [{'type': 'integer'}, {'type': 'null'}], 'default': None}, 'efficiency': {'default': 1.0, 'type': 'number'}}, 'required': ['operation'], 'type': 'object'}}}]}}
